From: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] FIPS wrapper for 7.x: only what the canister calls; derived in-canister check replaces the 6.12 driver-name lists

Linux 7.3-rc4 port of the Photon FIPS canister series.
See EXPERIMENTAL-7.3-rc4-FIPS.md for the per-patch decisions.
---
diff --git a/crypto/testmgr.c b/crypto/testmgr.c
index 55a28387a6281ddee09d3abb92467d4bca29bd04..2a961c26fe9765e32d3cb094f2ce822d2ac55903 100644
--- a/crypto/testmgr.c
+++ b/crypto/testmgr.c
@@ -5649,6 +5649,15 @@ static int alg_find_test(const char *alg)
  * allowed in FIPS mode and runs real vectors (not alg_test_null), so a
  * self-test table entry cannot pass vacuously.
  */
+/* Photon FIPS: testmgr's fips_allowed flag for @alg (false if untested). */
+bool alg_test_fips_allowed(const char *alg);
+bool alg_test_fips_allowed(const char *alg)
+{
+	int i = alg_find_test(alg);
+
+	return i >= 0 && alg_test_descs[i].fips_allowed;
+}
+
 bool alg_test_is_real_fips_test(const char *alg);
 bool alg_test_is_real_fips_test(const char *alg)
 {
